I love the idea, it makes the game a little more amusing and
intricate.  But, I don't like the implementation in this patch, it
makes the game harder in an annoying way (making something pretty much
unavailable is, I think, unnecessarily annoying).  I would say if you
have sleep resistance, you wake up pretty quickly and can go back to
reading.

This gives me another idea: identifying spellbooks when you fail to
read them successfully, by having one of the possible bad effects be
related to the spell that was in the book, instead of or in addition
to the possible generic effects you get now.
 - fail to read a spellbook of fire, effect same as a fire trap
 - fail to read a spellbook of polymorph, affected as if poly trap
 - fail to read charm monster, a nearby pet gets untamed
 - fail to read detect monsters, monsters on level detect you & aggravate
 - fail to read magic mapping, un-maps the current level
 - fail to read identify, partial amnesia (for objects only)
 ... etc. ...

Hmm, fail to read finger of death, and die?  That makes the whole
business much much more dangerous.  Maybe that one shouldn't happen
unless it's cursed, or maybe it should be changed to losing a level
(you lose some "life") - which would just muddle up the IDing a bit.
